      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UBETCHA TIGERPIE (10) was a real eye-catcher in last week's Len Smith Mile where he galloped out but charged home late for fourth. Had a series of second row barriers prior but did manage a very close second in the Geelong Cup. Cops the outside barrier but with manners and his A-game he can win from there. SINALOA (6) came from a similar barrier for a solid fourth in a decent line-up here last week. A repeat of that performance would measure up well here. PICCADILLY PETE NZ (7) came from this barrier to be beaten only 2m into third here last week. The longer trip is some query but he makes each way appeal. JUNGLE DRAGON (8) and BETTER ECLIPSE (9) are both going well enough to feature with even luck from wider draws.",
